<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="skill">bartering</ansi> (skill)

Bartering is the trader's craft: reading a merchant, knowing what a
thing is truly worth, and walking away with more coin in your pouch.
It is governed by <ansi fg="yellow">Charisma</ansi> — presence and persuasion move prices,
not muscle.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ What It Does ━━━</ansi>

  - Merchants charge you less when you <ansi fg="command">buy</ansi> and pay you better when
    you <ansi fg="command">sell</ansi>. The discount grows with your skill — a practiced
    trader keeps a noticeable slice of every deal.
  - <ansi fg="command">appraise</ansi> tells you what an item is worth before you commit to
    a trade.
  - <ansi fg="command">offer</ansi> lets you propose a trade to a merchant directly.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Skill Progression ━━━</ansi>

Bartering improves through use: buying, selling, and appraising all
teach it. There is no trainer — trade often and the knack comes.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Related Reading ━━━</ansi>

Shop stock and prices are a living economy: merchants run low, restock
over time, and charge more for what is scarce. Buying at the right
moment matters as much as haggling.

